Fast paths kept out of states they don't handle (2026-10-04 audit)

- drivers/osmesa/osmesa.c: OSMesa's own depth-tested triangles and flat
  lines write through osmesa->rowaddr, the window's (or OSMesaBuffer's)
  rows. riscos-speed made them depend on the bound framebuffer's depth
  format, so with a framebuffer object bound (any depth attachment, in a
  24-bit context too) they drew into the window instead, and crashed with
  an FBO larger than the window. They are now only used when the window
  system framebuffer is bound, and not with GL_DEPTH_CLAMP, which they
  don't apply.
- swrast/s_context.c: _NEW_TRANSFORM (depth clamp) revalidates the
  triangle function.
- swrast/s_triangle.c: under GL_FASTEST the fast textured triangles can
  use the magnification filter, so GL_CLAMP (which blends in the border
  colour with GL_LINEAR) is only taken when both filters are GL_NEAREST.

Checked by tests/host-harness/mesa/render-paths.c.

